{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-03T09:29:33.552Z","author":"pi-presets-qz1k-salvage-1103","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"c8c18d542b20d4ff8b026711","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-03T09:29:33.552Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-03T09:29:33.551Z","author":"pi-presets-qz1k-salvage-1103","text":"Salvage plan from the unmerged review work on the typed-binding item (leftover worktree diff, branch fix/typed-parameter-binding-review): (1) diffPreset refuses invalid_secret_reference when a sensitive legacy id_prefix would mint public seed ids; (2) diff --replace refuses invalid_secret_reference when sensitive legacy governance/validation/testing settings would enter isolated normalization history, and replacement normalization never copies a caller prefix into the scratch tracker; (3) diff and apply capture definition identity, settings, template documents, seed inventory, flags and resolved values once before any await, so mutating SDK accessors cannot change compared state (planner validates a record with undefined-sentinel semantics too); (4) the seed writer requires a withSeeds id to be a registered catalog member, refusing unknown and Object.prototype names before any write. Test-first: each behaviour gets a test that fails on current main, then the port. Each refusal is typed, leaves tracker bytes unchanged, and has a must-allow twin."}]}],"before_hash":"ef312de785773591a75a1217bc9f383a7001887718c0bfbe445d5c62f0b297e1","after_hash":"7faf088d84ee8a42937c800607709e77c80f9e326be532899e6567b4d930e4df","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"176aae624ec1a09a888856829586cb4efe57fa356744a1ea32e90b30bbc1440